{title: 034 - Wake the Song}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Worship}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]Wake the song of joy [Dm/F]and [Bb/F]gladness; [F]Hither [C7/G]bring your noblest [F]lays;
[F]Banish [Edim]every [Am/E]thought [F]of sadness, [Dm/F]Pouring [Bb/F]forth [F]your highest praise.
[F/A]Sing to Him whose [Bb/F]care [F]has brought [Gm/Bb]us [Dm/A]Once [C7/E]again with friends [G7]to [C]meet,
[F/C]And whose [C7]loving voice has taught us [Dm/A]Of [C]the way [F/C]to [G]Jesus' [C/G]feet.
[C]Wake the song, [F/C](wake the [Gm/Bb]song,) [Dm/A]wake the [C7/G]song, [Dm/F](wake the [F]song,)
[F]the song of joy and [Edim]gladness,
[C]Wake the song, (wake the song,) wake the [Dm]song, (wake the song,)
[F/C]The song [Gm/D]of Jubilee.

Refrain:
[Bb]Wake the [Am]song, wake the song,
[Dm]The song of joy [C]and gladness,
[Edim]Wake the [F]song, wake the song,
[Gm/Bb]The song of [F]Jubilee.

Verse 2:
[F]Joyfully [Bb/F]with [F]songs and [C7/G]banners,
[F]We [Edim]will [Am/E]greet [F]the [Dm/F]festal [F]day;
[F/A]Shout aloud our [Dm/A]glad [C7/E]hosannas,
[F/C]And [C7]our grateful [C]homage [G]pay.
[C]We will [F/C]chant [Gm/Bb]our [Dm/A]Savior's glory
[F]while our thoughts we raise [Edim]above,
[C]Telling still the old, old, [Dm]story,
[F/C]Precious [Gm/D]theme- redeeming love!

Verse 3:
[F]Thanks to Thee, [Bb/F]O [F]holy [C7/G]Father,
[F]For [Edim]the [Am/E]mercies [Dm/F]of [Bb/F]the [F]year;
[F/A]May each [Bb/F]heart, [F]as [Dm/A]here [C7/E]we gather,
[F/C]Swell [C7]with gratitude [F/C]sincere,
[C]Thanks to [F/C]Thee, [Gm/Bb]O [Dm/A]loving Savior,
[F]For redemption through [Edim]Thy [F]blood.
[C]Breathe upon us, Holy [Dm]Spirit,
[F/C]Sweetly [Gm/D]draw us near to God.
